From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Make the initial PHY bias vote program the system mux

Linux 7.3 adds a reference count for 7 nm PHY PLL bias access. The PHY enable
path starts with a vote and sets PLL_SHUTDOWNB directly. Subsequent prepare and
rate-query votes therefore skip the helper's first-vote hardware programming,
leaving PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES at zero after probe-time reads. On this Liuqin trial
both display links had the expected pixel/byte rates, frame CRCs changed for
linear colour/black patterns, and the panel answered GET_POWER_MODE with 0x9e,
but the display stayed blank. The PLL mux read zero instead of the working
6.17 value 0xc0.

Program the same system mux value when establishing the initial vote, and
clear it when the PHY's final shutdown clears all votes. Keep reference
counting, frequencies, lane timings, and panel commands unchanged. Source
regression tests exercise nested prepare/rate-query votes and repeated power
cycles, including negative controls from the failing source.

This is a candidate fix; hardware validation remains pending.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
index 301dc86238a..c0b84e222aa 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -1249,6 +1249,8 @@ static int dsi_7nm_phy_enable(struct msm_dsi_phy *phy,
 	data = DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_DIGTOP_PWRDN_B |
 	       DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_PLL_SHUTDOWNB;
 	writel(data, base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
+	/* The initial bias vote must program the same mux as later votes. */
+	writel(0xc0, phy->pll_base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
 
 	/* Assert PLL core reset */
@@ -1394,6 +1396,7 @@ static void dsi_7nm_phy_disable(struct msm_dsi_phy *phy)
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
 	pll->pll_enable_cnt = 0;
 	/* Turn off all PHY blocks */
+	writel(0, phy->pll_base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES);
 	writel(0x00, base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
 
